  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the laboratory, dinitrogen is prepared by treating an aqueous solution of ammonium chloride with sodium nitrite.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mi>Cl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>NaNO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>NaCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>",
